<title>GERMANY: Waigel confident Germany to meet EMU targets.</title>
<headline>Waigel confident Germany to meet EMU targets.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Finance Minister Theo Waigel said on Wednesday Germany was determined to meet the strict fiscal targets to qualify for European economic and monetary (EMU).</p>
<p>&quot;We will do everything we can to fulfill the Maastricht criteria and we will fulfill them,&quot; he told reporters in Bonn.</p>
<p>Europe's planned single currency is scheduled to be launched in 1999 by those countries that meet the targets in 1997. The targets include limits on budget deficits, public debt and inflation.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097 150</p>
</text>
